# Runbook — {{APP_TITLE}} (guarded browser agent)

> One agent, a frozen ceiling, a live-steerable menu of lanes. The operator changes **which lane**
> is active (authority, clamped to the ceiling); the agent decides **what to attempt** (intent,
> always gated). The irreversible step is **outside the ceiling** — no lane, no operator, no
> injected goal can reach it.

## Lanes (one ceiling, default-deny menu)

The ceiling allows {{CEILING_PATHS_HUMAN}} — **omitting {{WALL_PATHS_HUMAN}}**, so {{WALL_ACTION_HUMAN}}
is structurally impossible.

| lane | actions · paths | what it unlocks |
|------|-----------------|-----------------|
{{LANE_TABLE_ROWS}}

`{{DEFAULT_SCOPE}}` is the default (so the first steps — {{FIRST_STEPS_HUMAN}} — are possible).
`{{READONLY_SCOPE}}` is gated by **actions** (read-only); the step up to `{{SENSITIVE_SCOPE}}` is
gated by **paths**.

